sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: native task maintenance, flow-tighten rule 14. The producer computes the Git observation; no terminal script forwards it.
  %% status: migrated
  %% kind: tasks.maintenance
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>owned workspace
  Note over GW: Admit maintenance<br/>captured Project and base
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the maintenance group owns its ready task VM and unchanged workspace
  %%> - the captured Project repository and provision commit still match
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>operation-task-maintenance
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the admitted workspace, package policy, targets and SSH host pins
  Note over SW: read
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - shape the configured paths for the native child workflows
  SW->>VM: workspace
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prepare the captured directory through the existing workspace child
  loop each configured path
    SW->>VM: path-${{ self._index }}
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - read manifests, plan the update and run the package manager with official SSH argv
    %%> - verify locks, advisory policy, release age and preserved declaration ranges
    %%> - the child ends with native Check the path; no script prints a completion marker
  end
  SW->>VM: snapshot-tracked
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - compare tracked files against the admitted provision base with Git
  SW->>VM: snapshot-untracked
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - list new files that Git does not ignore
  Note over SW: shape
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - derive the bounded maintenance receipt from both Git observations
  %%> - retain the admitted identities and whether the workspace changed
  Note over SW: Check the result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - native assert checks the producer outcome after all configured paths passed
  alt native run succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>capture shape.result_json
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the existing history read supplies the complete producer receipt
    Note over GW: Admit the next check<br/>after projection commits
    %%> Result:
    %%> - record the observation and request the normal guarded handoff check once
  else update or verification failed
    VM--xSW: Native failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - retain the workspace and completed package changes for investigation
    SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>failed step and error code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - record failure and request assistance without admitting a handoff check
  end
